index d8b1f0603..f0b628bed 100644
--- a/packages/docs/content/docs/preview.mdx
+++ b/packages/docs/content/docs/preview.mdx
@@ -11,6 +11,8 @@ When you start a dev server, OpenChamber can open it right inside the app instea
 
 Open the browser panel from the globe button in the app header. If a dev server is already running, it is listed there and one click opens it — OpenChamber finds it by looking at what is actually listening on your machine, so it works no matter how you started it.
 
+The list shows the process command next to each address, and busy machines can carry a lot of listeners that are not your dev server. Hover a row to give the port a name — it stays on that port until you reset it — or to hide ports you never want to see.
+
 A dev server also opens automatically when:
 
 - you press **Open preview** on a local address in the terminal
